# Copy this file to .env and edit it. `docker compose` reads THIS file for
# both variable substitution in docker-compose.yml (${VAR} placeholders) and
# — via the quote-service `env_file:` — the container's own environment.
#
# NOTHING BELOW IS REQUIRED. `docker compose up` with an empty (or missing)
# .env still starts and answers requests — every provider key is optional,
# and every other setting has a documented default. Fill in what you need.

# ───────────────────────────── Origins (CORS) ──────────────────────────────
#
# REQUIRED for a browser to actually call this service — with no
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS set, the default is gibs's own production hostnames, which
# will not match yours. Comma-separated. Accepts `*` (any origin) and a
# single leading-label wildcard, e.g. `https://*.example.com` (matches
# `https://anything.example.com`, NOT `https://a.b.example.com` and not a
# look-alike suffix). `*` is convenient for local testing; name your real
# frontend origin(s) for anything else.

# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,https://your-frontend.example.com

# ─────────────────────────── Provider keys (optional) ──────────────────────
#
# Every provider works with NO key, at that provider's own public/anonymous
# rate limit — the server logs one startup warning naming whichever of these
# is unset, never a crash. Set what you have.

# LI.FI (https://li.fi) — raises the anonymous 75-quotes-per-2-hours limit.
# GIBS_LIFI_API_KEY is accepted as a legacy alias for this same variable.
# LIFI_API_KEY=

# The `integrator` string LI.FI attributes your traffic and any referral fee
# to. This service names no default of its own — an unset value simply omits
# the field. Only set this if LI.FI issued YOU an integrator string.
# LIFI_INTEGRATOR=

# Relay (https://relay.link) — raises Relay's own public rate limit.
# RELAY_API_KEY=

# NEAR Intents partner key, if you have one.
# NEAR_INTENTS_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────── Safety ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Comma-separated chain ids this instance must NEVER name in an outbound
# LI.FI/Relay/NEAR Intents request, in the address or the body, including
# the forwarding routes. Empty by default. Gibs's own deploy sets this to
# PulseChain's mainnet and testnet ids (369,943); if you are running your
# own bridge with a chain that must never reach a public quote aggregator,
# name it here.
# NEVER_SEND_CHAIN_IDS=

# ────────────────────────── Client identity source ─────────────────────────
#
# 'socket' (the default — leave this unset unless you have a specific
# reason) always keys rate limiting on the real TCP socket peer address,
# which a client cannot forge. This is the ONLY safe choice unless you are
# running your own trusted reverse proxy directly in front of this
# container on the SAME box, setting X-Client-IP from the real client
# address itself (Caddy's {client_ip}, nginx's $remote_addr, ...) — in that
# specific shape, set CLIENT_IP_SOURCE=proxy-header so rate limiting keys on
# the real client instead of your proxy's own address for every request.
# Setting this to proxy-header WITHOUT such a proxy lets any client bypass
# rate limiting entirely by sending a made-up X-Client-IP header.
# CLIENT_IP_SOURCE=socket

# ────────────────────────── Probe addresses (optional) ─────────────────────
#
# A server-held address, per ecosystem, this service names as its own
# fromAddress/recipient on a LI.FI/Relay pre-quote. These addresses never
# sign anything and never hold funds — but a wrong one asks a provider to
# quote against something it does not recognize rather than failing loudly,
# so use a real address you control. An ecosystem left unset here simply
# gets no display quotes for that ecosystem's leg; nothing crashes.
# PROBE_ADDRESS_EVM=
# PROBE_ADDRESS_SVM=
# PROBE_ADDRESS_BVM=
# PROBE_ADDRESS_TVM=
# PROBE_ADDRESS_TONVM=
# PROBE_ADDRESS_HYPEVM=
# PROBE_ADDRESS_ZCASH=

# ───────────────────────────────── Ports ────────────────────────────────
#
# The HOST port docker-compose.yml publishes the quote service on
# (127.0.0.1 by default — see README.md's "Expose it" section).
# QUOTE_SERVICE_PORT=8080

# ─────────────────────────────── Image tag ──────────────────────────────
#
# Which published tag of ghcr.io/gibsfinance/quote-service to pull. Leave
# unset for the most recent release. Pin a specific tag if you want your
# instance to stay on a known version between upgrades.
# QUOTE_SERVICE_IMAGE_TAG=latest
